I am outside now.
My suitcase is big and heavy.
There is a taxi.
I lift my suitcase into the taxi.
The driver is a friendly man.
"What is the address?" he asks.
"It is Nygade twelve," I say.
He nods and drives.
"Are you a tourist?" the driver asks.
"No, I am not a tourist," I answer.
"Where do you come from?" he asks.
"I come from Mexico," I say.
I smile.
I am very proud.
"I am a software engineer," I say.
"My new job is here in Copenhagen."
He smiles again.
"How exciting."
"Welcome to Denmark," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
